## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/sdfadjust.html
- Summary (EN): SDF Adjust modifies a Mono signed distance field layer to reshape its shape, with settings for iso offset, outline, absolute value and invert. It has one input and one output, both named sdf.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud SDF Adjust retouche une couche SDF mono pour en modifier la forme, avec décalage d'isovaleur, contour, valeur absolue et inversion.

- Inputs meaning: ["sdf: the SDF Mono layer to adjust"]

- Key parameters: ["Iso Offset: crossing point treated as the border; higher values enlarge the shape, lower values shrink it", "Outline: makes a hollow thin outline; the value sets the border thickness by taking the absolute value and subtracting it", "Absolute Value: converts negative values to positive, leaving only a thin border", "Invert: swaps positive and negative values"]

- Caveats: ["The page lists no explicit caveats", "The page does not say how other input types are handled"]

